WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:18.690
X eighteen is the Second Napoleon Point of triangle A B C: erect equilateral triangles inward on sides B C, C A, and A B, take their centroids Nap prime sub a, Nap prime sub b, and Nap prime sub c to form the inner Napoleon equilateral triangle, and the lines from A, B, and C to those three centers concur at X eighteen.

2
00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:26.997
Its trilinear coordinates are cosecant of A minus pi over six, to cosecant of B minus pi over six, to cosecant of C minus pi over six.

3
00:00:26.997 --> 00:00:37.120
Remarkably, the difference in area between the outer Napoleon triangle of X seventeen and the inner Napoleon triangle of X eighteen equals the exact area of triangle A B C!

4
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:47.740
X eighteen lies on lines X three X fourteen, X five X thirteen, X four X sixteen, and X six X seventeen, and is the isogonal conjugate of X sixty-two.
